WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:14.679
Bello: Your dad will be back soon, Brad.

2
00:00:14.699 --> 00:00:17.240
Brad: Yeah, any second, I suppose.

3
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.120
Danny: We have to hide Bello!

4
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.581
Bello: I’m not going to hide, Danny.

5
00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:25.622
Tina: You mean you’re going to let my neighbor see you?

6
00:00:25.642 --> 00:00:27.543
Tina: She’ll call the police.

7
00:00:27.563 --> 00:00:30.823
Bello: No, I mean it’s time for me to go back home.

8
00:00:30.844 --> 00:00:32.404
Danny: You’re leaving?

9
00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:33.925
Bello: And quickly.

10
00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:35.706
I can’t be caught here.

11
00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:38.568
Tina: I’m going to miss you.

12
00:00:38.588 --> 00:00:41.271
Chuck: We just met you!

13
00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:45.234
Bello: It was a lot of fun to visit your world again.

14
00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:50.618
Bello: I didn’t like being small very much, but it was a great adventure.

15
00:00:50.638 --> 00:00:56.022
Tina: Come on, you guys can say good-bye too.

16
00:00:56.042 --> 00:00:59.946
Dave: How are you going to get back, Bello?

17
00:00:59.966 --> 00:01:04.692
Bello: All it takes is a little magic and a little imagination.

18
00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:11.294
Chuck: Bello, if you could go at any time, why didn’t you leave [n3@when you were in trouble?

19
00:01:11.314 --> 00:01:14.275
Bello: Tina brought me here so that I could help.

20
00:01:14.295 --> 00:01:17.536
Bello: I couldn’t leave until everything was all right.

21
00:01:17.556 --> 00:01:21.197
Bello: Now, I think everything is better than it was before.

22
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:25.098
Bello: Danny, do you have any nano-putty left?

23
00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.199
Danny: I don’t know.

24
00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.939
Tina: Here’s some.

25
00:01:29.959 --> 00:01:31.540
Bello: Good.

26
00:01:32.736 --> 00:01:38.259
When Danny, Tina, and Brad first came [n3@to my world, they used magic clay.

27
00:01:38.279 --> 00:01:41.141
Bello: It looked a lot like this nano-putty.

28
00:01:41.821 --> 00:01:42.822
Chuck: Magic clay?

29
00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.462
Bello: Yes.

30
00:01:44.342 --> 00:01:50.866
Bello: When they used the clay and their imaginations, they were [n3@able to go on a magical journey.

31
00:01:50.886 --> 00:01:54.428
Dave: I’d love to hear the story of your adventures.

32
00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:56.829
Danny: I’m sure I can tell you one day.

33
00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:03.816
Danny: You see, first, we had to make a key from the magic clay— Bello: Do you mean

34
00:02:03.877 --> 00:02:05.057
a key like this one?

35
00:02:05.077 --> 00:02:08.400
Mrs. Rice: Ahh!

36
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.022
Bello: Good-bye, everyone.

37
00:02:12.623 --> 00:02:13.303
Take care.

38
00:02:13.323 --> 00:02:15.365
The kids: Good-bye, Bello.

39
00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:25.132
Mrs. Rice: There!

40
00:02:25.372 --> 00:02:26.012
You saw it too!

41
00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:28.774
Mr. Joseph: Where did that flashlight go?

42
00:02:29.435 --> 00:02:30.836
It must be here somewhere.

43
00:02:32.492 --> 00:02:34.674
Brad: We must have blown another fuse, Dad.

44
00:02:34.694 --> 00:02:37.316
Mr. Joseph: I’m almost losing my patience, Brad.

45
00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.583
Rice: Where’s the but there was a Mrs.

46
00:02:45.223 --> 00:02:46.945
Rice: I could have sworn I saw a Mr.

47
00:02:46.965 --> 00:02:49.046
Joseph: We must have imagined it.

48
00:02:49.607 --> 00:02:51.308
There’s no such thing as giants.

49
00:02:52.189 --> 00:02:54.351
Mr. Joseph: It’s quite messy in here, Brad.

50
00:02:54.391 --> 00:02:56.112
Brad: Sorry, Dad.

51
00:02:56.132 --> 00:02:57.414
We’ll clean it up.

52
00:02:58.094 --> 00:02:59.215
We were just playing.
